## 4. Validation checklist

| # | Host | Command | Expected |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Target | `sudo ufw status verbose` | `Status: active`, `Default: deny (incoming), deny (outgoing), deny (routed)` |
| 2 | Target | `sudo ufw status numbered` | Inbound rule: only `22/tcp` from `10.10.10.10`; outbound: the five allows |
| 3 | Bastion | `sudo ufw status verbose` | Same defaults; the `deny out to HOST_VMNET8_IP` rule is **#1** |
| 4 | Bastion | `ssh target 'hostname'` | Works |
| 5 | Bastion | `sudo apt update` | Works |
| 6 | Target | `curl -sI -m 8 https://archive.ubuntu.com \| head -1` (NAT connected) | HTTP status line returned |
| 7 | Target | `ping -c 1 -W 2 1.1.1.1` | Fails |
| 8 | Target | `curl -m 5 http://example.com:8080` | Fails |
| 9 | Bastion | `curl -m 5 http://HOST_VMNET8_IP` | Fails (blocked by rule #1) |
| 10 | Target → Bastion | Step D.1 test | Times out |
| 11 | Bastion → Target | Step D.2 test | Times out |
| 12 | Target | `sudo journalctl -k --no-pager \| grep 'UFW BLOCK' \| tail -3` | Block entries present |
| 13 | Target | fail2ban ban/unban | Still works |
| 14 | Both | `systemctl is-enabled ufw` and `sudo ufw status` after reboot | `enabled` and `active` |
| 15 | Target | `ip route` after closing NAT | No default route |
| 16 | Both | `systemctl list-timers 'ufw-rollback*'` | Nothing (timer cancelled) |

